A rower at $P$ is $3$ km from the nearest point $A$ on a straight shore, and wants to reach $B$, which is $8$ km along the shore from $A$.
She rows at $3$ km/h to a point $x$ km from $A$, then walks the rest at $5$ km/h.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}]
\usetikzlibrary{calc}
\coordinate (A) at (0,0);
\coordinate (P) at (0,2.25);
\coordinate (L) at (3.0,0);
\coordinate (B) at (6,0);
\draw (-0.5,0) -- (6.5,0);
\draw (A) -- (P) node[midway, left] {$3$ km};
\draw (P) -- (L);
\draw (A) -- (L) node[midway, below] {$x$ km};
\draw (L) -- (B) node[midway, below] {$8 - x$ km};
\coordinate (a) at ($(A)!0.3cm!(B)$);
\coordinate (b) at ($(A)!0.3cm!(P)$);
\draw (a) -- ($(a)+(b)-(A)$) -- (b);
\node[above] at (P) {$P$};
\node[above left] at (A) {$A$};
\node[above right] at (B) {$B$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]
Show that the total time is $T = \dfrac{\sqrt{9 + x^{2}}}{3} + \dfrac{8 - x}{5}$ hours, then find the value of $x$ that minimises $T$.

A pipeline runs from a well $W$, which is $4$ km from a straight road, to a depot $D$, which is $15$ km along the road from the point $N$ nearest $W$.
Off-road pipe costs $\$50\,000$ per km and pipe laid along the road costs $\$30\,000$ per km.
The pipeline meets the road $x$ km from $N$.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}]
\usetikzlibrary{calc}
\coordinate (N) at (0,0);
\coordinate (W) at (0,1.4);
\coordinate (M) at (1.6,0);
\coordinate (D) at (5.25,0);
\draw (-0.5,0) -- (5.75,0);
\draw (N) -- (W) node[midway, left] {$4$ km};
\draw (W) -- (M);
\draw (N) -- (M) node[midway, below] {$x$ km};
\draw (M) -- (D) node[midway, below] {$15 - x$ km};
\coordinate (a) at ($(N)!0.3cm!(D)$);
\coordinate (b) at ($(N)!0.3cm!(W)$);
\draw (a) -- ($(a)+(b)-(N)$) -- (b);
\node[above] at (W) {$W$};
\node[above left] at (N) {$N$};
\node[above right] at (D) {$D$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]
Find the value of $x$ that minimises the total cost.
